IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pf75-nouns`
IMPORT `pf75-cross-references`

-- Row il-75. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS: the sound readings kept beside the two items. They pass.
-- Each control shows that the test used in pf75-tests-red.l4 finds what it looks for where it is there, so that a failing test in that module records what the pages print and is not a test that cannot succeed.
-- The expected values are written from the quotation lines in pf75-cross-references.l4 and from the printed pages, not copied from the values there.

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- I1 control 1: the test finds an end date where one is printed. The words of subsection (He) hold the words that give the end and the Hebrew form of the date; the date typed is 31 March 2018; the question the red module asks, asked the other way round, finds the subsection in the list.
#ASSERT `the end date is found in the words that print it` `the end date printed in 24A(he)`
#ASSERT `the end date printed in 24A(he)`'s `the date it prints` EQUALS Date 31 3 2018
#ASSERT `the section prints a subsection that ends it on a stated date` `section 24A` `the end dates printed in the Law, as deposited here`

-- I1 control 2: the words of item 13A, as SH 2507 printed them, contain both pointers, and each pointer is among the words of the text that holds it.
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `item 13A as printed in SH 2507` "24א(ב)(8)"
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `item 13A as printed in SH 2507` "24ב(א)(11)"
#ASSERT CONTAINS (`the first pointer of item 13A`'s `the printed text that holds it`'s `its words`) (`the first pointer of item 13A`'s `its words as printed`)
#ASSERT CONTAINS (`the second pointer of item 13A`'s `the printed text that holds it`'s `its words`) (`the second pointer of item 13A`'s `its words as printed`)

-- I1 control 3: section 24A and the Schedule item as worded in SH 2507 have the same printed commencement date, 1 April 2016, in one provision.
#ASSERT `the commencement names the place` `the commencement of section 24A and of item 13A as worded in sections 11 and 23 of SH 2507` `section 24A`
#ASSERT `the commencement names the place` `the commencement of section 24A and of item 13A as worded in sections 11 and 23 of SH 2507` `item 13A of Part B of the First Schedule`
#ASSERT `the commencement of section 24A and of item 13A as worded in sections 11 and 23 of SH 2507`'s `the date it prints` EQUALS Date 1 4 2016

-- I1 control 4: the end date printed in subsection (He) is later than that commencement date.
#ASSERT `the end date printed in 24A(he)`'s `the date it prints` > `the commencement of section 24A and of item 13A as worded in sections 11 and 23 of SH 2507`'s `the date it prints`

-- I1 control 5: item 13A and subsection (He) were printed in the same issue, SH 2507.
#ASSERT `the two instruments are the same issue` (`item 13A as printed in SH 2507`'s `the instrument that printed it`) (`subsection (he) of section 24A as printed in SH 2507`'s `the instrument that printed it`)

-- I2 control 1: the test finds the letter Gimel where it is cited. The order cites 34Vav(Gimel), and subsection (Gimel) is printed in SH 2932 on page 57.
#ASSERT `the section prints the letter the citation names` `the citation of 34Vav(gimel) in the order` `section 34Vav as printed in SH 2932`
#ASSERT `every citation of the section names a letter the section prints` `section 34Vav as printed in SH 2932` (LIST `the citation of 34Vav(gimel) in the order`)

-- I2 control 2: section 34Vav itself is printed in the same issue as the definition: the cited section is among the pages deposited here.
#ASSERT `the two instruments are the same issue` (`section 34Vav as printed in SH 2932`'s `the instrument that printed it`) (`the definition of the determining date as printed in SH 2932`'s `the instrument that printed it`)

-- I2 control 3: the words of subsection (Gimel) contain the term the definition defines.
#ASSERT `the printed text contains the words` `subsection (gimel) of section 34Vav as printed in SH 2932` "המועד הקובע"

-- I2 control 4: the date printed in the definition, 1 July 2022, is earlier than the date printed in the order, 1 October 2022.
#ASSERT `the first date is earlier than the second` `the date printed in the definition` `the date printed in the order`
